SUMMARY:Perry Rudnick Nature Tr\; a Walk
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\n**A WALK IN THE PARK.**\nWe will Tour de Pa
 rks of the area. One at a time.\n**THIS WEEK: Perry Rudnick Nature Tr in K
 ellogg Preserve**\nWe are the Sloth Walking Team: “We will get there whe
 n we get there.”\n**The Curmudgeon will lead this event. Up to 12 ppl** 
 are welcome to join us.\n**https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bsh_8qxUfDY**\n
 Length: 1.4 mi\; Accum ascent: 100 ft. Walking sticks recommended.\nDrive 
 time: 15 min\n**Limited Parking\; Carpooling necessary.**\nGoogle Map = 
 “Kellogg Nature Trails”\nApprx return time: 12 noon (=1.75hrs)\n**(Thi
 s event is NOT for beginners or those with health or balance issues.)**\n*
 *Optional: Some of us will lunch after the walk.**\nWeather Check: Henders
 onville\, NC.\nCarpool contributions appreciated. $1.00 suggested\nDifficu
 lty: Moderate\; with roots on an earthen tr. **1 very short steep section.
 ** Sturdy shoes suggested. Suitable for almost everyone. NOT suitable for 
 those with balance issues.\nWAITLISTED PEOPLE WILL BE ADDED AS DRIVERS SIG
 N ON.\nI currently have 3.5 driver(s). (=14ppl)\nWe suggest open windows w
 hile carpooling. Only you know your own health status so judge accordingly
  if an event may endanger your health or the health of others.\nPlease bri
 ng an extra pair of shoes to avoid bringing your muddy shoes into the driv
 er's car at the end of the hike.\nIncessant prattlers will be assumed to b
 e having an affair. My attempts to quiet the prattlers has failed. This ha
 s become a ‘social networking’ event.\n**This is a dog-participant wal
 k.** This event is NOT for those who are uncomfortable with the antics of 
 fun-loving dogs. Dogs are welcome (IF their masters are well trained). 'On
  leash' rules apply. Small (lap)dogs may carpool. Large dogs will drive th
 emselves.\n**DESCRIPTION\;**\nRemember - hikes led by ‘the Curmudgeon’
  tend to have challenging surprises.\nWood elves are mischievous\; Zip you
 r backpacks tight.\nThe 1.5 mile trail meanders through three distinct eco
 systems—trillium and fern wetland\, hardwood forest with rhododendron an
 d mountain laurel\, and wildflower meadow. Various art sculptures are scat
 tered throughout.\nAll walks are at your own risk. You are responsible for
  your OWN safety and adequate equipment.\nWaiver: The organizer of this ev
 ent is a volunteer and not a professional guide. The function of the organ
 izer is only to organize this event. There are certain risks inherent in a
 ny outdoor activity. Each participant\, by signing up to attend this event
 \, agrees to release from liability the leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, it
 s Partners\, Affiliates\, and members for any accident\, injury\, illness\
 , or personal loss which might occur while participating in this activity 
 or while traveling in any vehicle during this trip. Each participant furth
 er agrees to abide by the rules and regulations concerning safety\, to fol
 low instructions of the leader(s)\, and not to become intentionally separa
 ted from the group. The leader(s) also has the right to use any images col
 lected on this trip for recording on website photo collections.\ngordie's 
 contact: CurmudgeonHiker@gmail.com\n(**before** day of hike): 828.393.0297
  (text only)\n**Pics: https://www.flickr.com/photos/146993931@N05/albums**
